      "created_at": "2026-09-25T04:42:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-25T04:42:00Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "ACK [f2a0db6](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36329/commits/f2a0db6309681c8ddc2963f34fb8519441f6668f)\r\n\r\nI tested the code locally and also did some code tracing to understand that the updates to combiner test are meant to run an additional test case where the last psbt is the first processed. The purpose is to ensure that no matter the order the psbts are processed, the underlying merge logic is order-independent\r\n\r\nPersonal note: I now understand that the combinepsbt method uses dynamic dispatch to handle the RPC command \"combinepsbt\" received by the node and runs the C++ code from psbt.cpp line 838 where the merge takes place.\r\n\r\nThe addition of the invalid psbt test data with <valuesize> not matching the expected <valuedata> for the psbt, checks that this code from psbt.h line 134 runs with expected behavior:\r\n\r\n`if (remaining_after + expected_size != remaining_before) {\r\n        throw std::ios_base::failure(\"Size of value was not the stated size\");`",
      "user": {
        "login": "aaron-leeb",
        "id": 156447042,
        "node_id": "U_kgDOCVMxQg",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/156447042?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/aaron-leeb",
